= The new future arises

...

The neverending crowd of mumbling social democrats, union members, Reichsbanner units, and our allies. The world's horizon opens upon me. On top of the stadium stands Carlo Mierendorff, our bravest member, one of the organizers of the Iron Front, and recently appointed one of the main ideologues following Hilferding's reputational collapse. Centrists have long been ousted, and their power has diminished over time with the new influx of youth.

​The roar of neorevisionism. The scream of the energized crowd. Mierendorff yells: "The future of social democracy lies in its reenergization, in its naturalization amongst the minds of the German collective, community, people. The bureaucratic mind of the party has never understood this. Ever-lustful labor has never eyed anything beyond its wealth and weight. The left has been anything but true action. State politicians have been greedy for too long. Listen to me, people of Germany. This day, we will denounce the old ways of socialism—the one that corrupted elder, selfish unions and ineffective bureaucracy under the palm of youth. The YOUTH—the driving force of every movement, the energy that gives movements a new breath, the future upon which the past must rely. Inseparably, this also means we must eventually abandon old conceptions and perceptions of the world, such as Marxism. What remains now is—socialism of the youth, of the nation, of the state, of the people."

​After a short break, Mierendorff declares:

​"The Hofgeismar congress... begins."

​...

​Huh.
​
My eyes, after opening up to the light, take in the newspaper's headline: "Carlo Mierendorff is elected as SPD party leader, officially replacing collective rule."
​...
